{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFive mixed infrastructure files contain repeated, stale, or misleading comments identified by the audit and revalidated on current `origin/main`. User-facing shell help remains complete; the remediation targets only redundant internal explanation.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve Terraform, shell, and systemd behavior byte-for-byte. Leave user-facing help complete and correct.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/bootstrap/main.tf` — Preserve local-state, one-time creation of remote-state prerequisites, `prevent_destroy`, and the requirement to migrate main Terraform state before removing the guard or destroying the bucket.\n- `infra/github/apply-mirror-lock.sh` — Preserve complete user-facing flags/defaults/authentication/destructive effects; main-and-tag locks, sole deploy-key bypass, preconditions, optional legacy removal, and recovery pointer.\n- `infra/github/rollback-mirror-lock.sh` — Preserve complete user-facing help and actual default behavior: delete both lock rulesets and recreate main protection; `--disable` is the non-deleting mode. Preserve snapshot dependency and explicit feature restoration.\n- `infra/systemd/rebar-autodeploy.service` — Preserve timer cadence, storm guard, environment overrides, health endpoint, fail-safe nonzero behavior, and `TimeoutStartSec=90` below the two-minute timer period so a hung clone cannot prevent rearming.\n- `infra/terraform-github/main.tf` — Preserve main-only lock, deploy-key bypass, no repository resource, bypass-key precondition, imported ownership, and intentional divergence from the shell fallback, which also locks tags. Out-of-scope stale parity prose is tracked by `wolfish-monarchist-maiasaura`.\n\nConsumers are Terraform/GitHub operators, shell users, and systemd.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the five declared files; user-facing help remains complete and accurate.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, historical, or stale prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Focused mirror-lock/systemd tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass; no missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, focused infrastructure tests, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788602476413113001,"uuid":"290598e0-b56d-4177-92c7-20adb12886f6"}